amp; accounting</strong> structures, scaling HORECA sector sales by 25% through strategic channel alignment.</li>\n    <li>Streamlined digital campaign architectures by translating ambiguous client requests into precise development tasks, accelerating customer acquisition velocity by 30%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "certifications_html": "<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Advanced Data Analytics</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Google Project Management</span><span class=\"cert-date\">In Progress</span></div>\n<div class=\"cert-row\"><span class=\"cert-name\">Coursera - Tableau Business Intelligence Analyst Professional Certificate</span><span class=\"cert-date\">May 2025</span></div>", "education_html": "<div class=\"edu-row\"><span>University of Delhi, B.Comm(Hons.)</span><span class=\"edu-date\">2013 \u2013 2016</span></div>", "hobbies_html": "<div class=\"hobbies-line\">Practicing Buddhism &nbsp;|&nbsp; Automating life with n8n &nbsp;|&nbsp; Growing Mushrooms</div>"}, "clSections": {"hasStoredCl": true, "salutation_html": "<div class=\"letter-meta\">\n  <div class=\"letter-date\">September 29, 2026</div>\n  <div class=\"recipient-block\">\n    <div>Hiring Team</div><div>Turing</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"subject-line\"><strong>Subject: Application for the Technical Business Analyst Role</strong></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager,</p>", "para1_hook_html": "<p>I am writing to apply for the Technical Business Analyst role at Turing. What stood out to me in the job description is the focus on turning messy day-to-day operations into clean requirements and clear reports. Before spending the last five years in data analytics, I ran my own small marketing agency for ten years. That mix taught me how much time teams lose when numbers do not match across different tools. Fixing those gaps between business users and engineering is the part of the job I enjoy most.</p>", "para2_stewardship_html": "<p>Outside of writing SQL queries and building Tableau dashboards, I spend my free time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating small daily tasks with n8n. Growing mushrooms in North India is not a fancy hobby. It comes down to watching basic details closely. If moisture or airflow slips even a little, the whole batch fails. I bring that same habit to my work when I check data quality, map workflows, or build reports that leaders rely on.</p>", "para3_impact_story_html": "<p>I also believe analysis is only useful when it solves a real problem on the ground. At Concentrix, our hiring data showed that new joiners were struggling once they started work. Sending another dashboard to management was not fixing the issue. I looked closely at the hiring steps and worked with leadership to bring our training team directly into the interview stage. That simple change improved hire quality by 84 percent. In my current role at Highspring India, I use the same practical approach across four engineering teams to automate recurring reports and cut manual work by 40 percent.</p>", "para4_resilience_html": "<p>My day-to-day work covers SQL, Python, Tableau, and working closely with business and tech teams. If the team at Turing uses an internal tool I have not worked with yet, I learn new systems quickly. Practical challenges early in my career taught me how to stay resourceful, focus on the basics, and get things done without hand-holding. When I take ownership of a task, nobody has to follow up twice.</p>", "para5_closing_html": "<p>I would welcome the chance to bring this steady, practical approach to Turing. Thank you for your time and consideration, and I look forward to speaking with you soon.</p>"}, "index": 4, "role": "Technical Business Analyst", "category": "technical_business_analyst", "jobUrl": "https://careers.turing.com/roles", "jdSnippet": "About the Role\nTuring is seeking a Technical Business Analyst who can operate comfortably in two worlds at once: the day-to-day realities of Operations and Finance, and the practical constraints of building software. This is a role for someone who listens deeply, asks sharp quest", "lastUpdate": "2026-10-06 09:00 IST", "referralName": "", "referralContact": "", "referralStatus": "", "resumeFileId": "1x9TYlpeTRP5-fxiqjbwhR2ivstKQUruo", "resumeUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clFileId": "1-pSNu7d4lV0jIdNsxSEUYLzI7equaBOl", "clUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "sections": {"summary": "<p>Technical Business Analyst combining finance and operations leadership to bridge complex back-office workflows with engineering execution. Expert in translating ambiguous business requirements into <strong>User Stories &amp; Acceptance Criteria</strong> for <strong>Agile Delivery</strong>. Proven ability to align technical constraints with <strong>Auditability &amp; Controls</strong> to accelerate software delivery without sacrificing financial integrity.</p>", "skills_html": "<ul>\n  <li><strong>Requirements Engineering & Database Management:</strong> PostgreSQL, MySQL, API/Data integration, BigQuery, Python (Pandas, NumPy)</li>\n  <li><strong>Process Optimization & Data Governance:</strong> Automating workflows, identifying improvement opportunities, data cleaning, wrangling, transformation, quality assurance</li>\n  <li><strong>Business Intelligence & Reporting:</strong> Tableau, Power BI, dashboard/report automation, interactive dashboards, narrative insight synthesis, executive presentations</li>\n  <li><strong>Stakeholder Collaboration & Soft Skills:</strong> Communication, cross-functional teamwork, client engagement, business acumen, critical thinking, problem solving, consulting, training</li>\n</ul>", "exp1_bullets": "<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Sr. Data Analyst, Highspring India \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Oct 2025 - Present</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Managed complex <strong>requirements engineering</strong> sessions across 4+ stakeholder groups to define transformation rules for pipelines processing 1M+ monthly records.</li>\n    <li>Executed <strong>process mapping</strong> initiatives for 3+ operational workflows, cutting manual overhead by 40% while preserving 95% delivery quality across 15+ launches.</li>\n    <li>Conducted <strong>data flows &amp; API concepts</strong> audits and gap analysis using basic <strong>SQL basics</strong> to resolve 500+ discrepancies, improving stability by 30%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Lead Trainer, Concentrix Daksh \u2013 Gurugram, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>April 2022 \u2013 Aug 2025</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Spearheaded structural workflow optimization through comprehensive <strong>back office operations</strong> analysis, boosting hire quality by 84% via <strong>user stories &amp; acceptance criteria</strong>.</li>\n    <li>Deployed self-serve operational metrics using <strong>stakeholder management</strong> strategies, closing knowledge gaps by 30% and lifting team productivity by 25%.</li>\n    <li>Facilitated <strong>UAT coordination</strong> and <strong>agile delivery</strong> cycles for internal HR tools, ensuring rigorous compliance and <strong>auditability &amp; controls</strong> standards.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\">\n    <span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span>\n    <span class=\"job-date\"><strong>Jan 2010 \u2013 Mar 2022</strong></span>\n  </div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed end-to-end client engagements focusing on <strong>finance &amp; accounting</strong> structures, scaling HORECA sector sales by 25% through strategic channel alignment.</li>\n    <li>Streamlined digital campaign architectures by translating ambiguous client requests into precise development tasks, accelerating customer acquisition velocity by 30%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<div class=\"letter-meta\">\n  <div class=\"letter-date\">September 29, 2026</div>\n  <div class=\"recipient-block\">\n    <div>Hiring Team</div><div>Turing</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"subject-line\"><strong>Subject: Application for the Technical Business Analyst Role</strong></div>\n</div>\n<p class=\"salutation\">Dear Hiring Manager,</p>\n<p>I am writing to apply for the Technical Business Analyst role at Turing. What stood out to me in the job description is the focus on turning messy day-to-day operations into clean requirements and clear reports. Before spending the last five years in data analytics, I ran my own small marketing agency for ten years. That mix taught me how much time teams lose when numbers do not match across different tools. Fixing those gaps between business users and engineering is the part of the job I enjoy most.</p>\n<p>Outside of writing SQL queries and building Tableau dashboards, I spend my free time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating small daily tasks with n8n. Growing mushrooms in North India is not a fancy hobby. It comes down to watching basic details closely. If moisture or airflow slips even a little, the whole batch fails. I bring that same habit to my work when I check data quality, map workflows, or build reports that leaders rely on.</p>\n<p>I also believe analysis is only useful when it solves a real problem on the ground. At Concentrix, our hiring data showed that new joiners were struggling once they started work. Sending another dashboard to management was not fixing the issue. I looked closely at the hiring steps and worked with leadership to bring our training team directly into the interview stage. That simple change improved hire quality by 84 percent. In my current role at Highspring India, I use the same practical approach across four engineering teams to automate recurring reports and cut manual work by 40 percent.</p>\n<p>My day-to-day work covers SQL, Python, Tableau, and working closely with business and tech teams. If the team at Turing uses an internal tool I have not worked with yet, I learn new systems quickly. Practical challenges early in my career taught me how to stay resourceful, focus on the basics, and get things done without hand-holding. When I take ownership of a task, nobody has to follow up twice.</p>\n<p>I would welcome the chance to bring this steady, practical approach to Turing. Thank you for your time and consideration, and I look forward to speaking with you soon.</p>"}, {"sNo": "5", "sNoNum": 5, "resumeId": "RES-5", "company": "Stripe", "industry": "Payments", "jobId": "N/A", "title": "Payments Analyst", "jd": "As a Technical Operations Analyst on the Payments team, you will own the reliability and accuracy of some of the world's most critical payment flows, a platform processing hundreds of billions of dollars annually. You will sit at the intersection of engineering, finance, and operations: triaging live payment failures, driving reconciliation accuracy, and partnering with financial institutions globally to resolve issues fast.\n\nThis is not a passive monitoring role. You will be expected to independently own investigations end-to-end, identify systemic issues before they escalate, and drive process improvements that scale with Stripe's growth.\n\nResponsibilities\nOwn reconciliation and payments-related investigations, ensuring accurate ledgering of funds and resolving discrepancies with banking partners swiftly and precisely.\nProactively monitor payment performance across users and payment me", "location": "Bengaluru", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://stripe.com/careers/search", "statu