uirements evolve quickly and cross-functional clarity is essential. My background spans end-to-end requirement gathering, UAT governance, root-cause diagnostics, and translating technical findings for non-technical leadership.</p>\n<p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in SQL, Python, Tableau, and business analysis can support United's upcoming initiatives.</p>"}, {"sNo": "10", "sNoNum": 10, "resumeId": "RES-10", "company": "United", "industry": "Airlines", "jobId": "Job IdGGN00002647", "title": "Analyst - Catering Systems Administrator", "jd": "Description\nJob Overview and Responsibilities\n\nThe Analyst - Catering Systems Administrator plays a critical role in maintaining the integrity and accuracy of catering data across United\u2019s systems and tools. This position supports business partners in delivering seamless catering services for flights systemwide through meticulous data management, system administration, and process optimization.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n\u2022 Data Management & Quality Assurance: Enter, verify, and maintain accurate catering data in United\u2019s management systems, ensuring timely updates with the precision required to support operational excellence\n\n\u2022 System Architecture & Configuration: Design and build system framework and codes to optimize service scheduling and ensure accurate vendor payments across the catering network\n\n\u2022 Data Integrity & Error Resolution: Conduct comprehensive data audits, identify inconsist", "location": "Gurugram, Haryana, India", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://careers.united.com/us/en/c/corporate-jobs", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Ready for Review", "combinedDocStatus": "To be reviewed", "appliedOn": "8/25/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "8/25/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "reference": "", "hrName": "", "hrEma