ormance metrics, accelerating ticket resolution speed by 35% across high-volume queues.</li>\n    <li>Analyzed user interaction trends to identify recurring <strong>service bottlenecks</strong>, partnering with operations leads to streamline workflows and boost customer satisfaction.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"job-block\">\n  <div class=\"job-header\"><span class=\"job-title\"><strong>Founder | Creative Director, Maerke Stratcomm \u2013 New Delhi, India</strong></span><span class=\"job-date\"><strong>June 2010 \u2013 July 2020</strong></span></div>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Directed <strong>commercial analytics</strong>, pricing strategy, and market segmentation for 15+ B2B and retail clients, driving a 30% increase in customer acquisition.</li>\n    <li>Implemented <strong>funnel performance tracking</strong> and ROI attribution models across regional distribution channels, expanding HORECA and enterprise account revenue by 25%.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>", "exp2_bullets": "", "exp3_bullets": ""}, "clHtml": "<p class=\"salutation\"><strong>To the Hiring Team at United,</strong></p>\n<p>What caught my attention about the <strong>Analyst - Catering Systems Administrator</strong> role at United is how directly it addresses the behind-the-scenes precision required to keep a massive operational network moving. Ensuring accurate data, vendor payments, and seamless system configurations across flight catering requires an analytical eye that respects how small data errors compound at scale. Having spent the last several years turning messy operational workflows into clean data models and structured BI\u2014preceded by a decade running my own commercial operations and B2B sales\u2014I know that logistical reliability lives or dies in the details of the database.</p>\n<p>When I am not writing <strong>SQL</strong> queries, mapping workflows, or auditing data consistency, I spend my spare time on my terrace in Gurugram growing mushrooms and automating personal workflows with <strong>n8n</strong>. Cultivating mushrooms in North India's climate is an exercise in strict variable control\u2014if humidity, airflow, or substrate prep drifts even slightly, the batch fails. I bring that exact same practical stewardship to enterprise systems, whether I am managing <strong>data integrity and error resolution</strong>, configuring system frameworks, or ensuring meticulous accuracy in daily operations.</p>\n<p>Furthermore, I believe data management is only as useful as the operational alignment it drives. During my time at Concentrix, our workforce data kept flagging quality drops in new training cohorts, and simply sending leadership another dashboard wasn\u2019t solving it. I dug into the recruitment funnel, traced the disconnect between screening and floor realities, and successfully advocated to embed our training team directly into the hiring workflow\u2014a structural shift that drove an <strong>84% improvement in hire quality</strong>. I apply that same cross-functional problem-solving today at Highspring India, partnering across <strong>4+ engineering and business groups</strong> to cut manual reporting overhead by 40% and resolve hundreds of data consistency gaps.</p>\n<p>While my technical foundation across SQL, Python, and data governance is robust, I understand that adapting to proprietary airline and catering management architectures requires a steep learning curve on day one. Early in my career, navigating real-world constraints taught me how to strip away noise, focus on fundamentals, and become a <strong>dedicated learner with a sharp focus</strong> on operational excellence. Above all, I am <strong>unconditionally dependable</strong>\u2014when I take ownership of a system or dataset, you will never have to chase me to see it through.</p>\n<p>I would value the chance to bring this grounded ownership, rigorous attention to detail, and steady execution to your team at United.</p><p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to discussing how my experience can support your upcoming data and systems initiatives.</p>"}, {"sNo": "11", "sNoNum": 11, "resumeId": "RES-11", "company": "University of Phoenix", "industry": "University", "jobId": "7531", "title": "Student Account Analyst", "jd": "About the Position\n\n\nThe Student Account Analyst performs financial and operational research and account analyses of student accounts to ensure students\u2019 billing invoices align with the terms and provisions of any enrollment, tuition assistance or other agreements that affect students\u2019 invoices.  Additionally, an individual audits various reports to ensure compliance with University policies and regulatory guidelines. A Student Account Analyst prepares daily accounting reconciliations, processes payments and refunds, and prepares various accounting transactions in accordance with University policy and generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP).\n\n What You\u2019ll Do:\nProduce routine and/or ad-hoc reports, using data extraction techniques, to audit student accounts and identify any required adjustments, including verification and application of tuition reduction benefits when applicable. ", "location": "US-AZ - Phoenix (Remote)", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://uop.avature.net/careers/SearchJobs", "status": "Applied", "stageBucket": "Applied", "resumeStatus": "Ready for Review", "clStatus": "Ready for Review", "combinedDocStatus": "To be reviewed", "appliedOn": "8/25/2026", "followUpDate": "", "createdOn": "8/25/2026 09:00 IST", "lastUpdated": "2026-10-07 15:15 IST", "reference": "", "hrName": "", "hrEmail": "", "hrPhone": "", "reviewerNotes": "", "clNotes": "", "generalNotes": "", "aboutCompany": "Online and campus higher education institution.", "resumeDriveId": "1PDWuVG3wILVLrgAPjR6dm91s8TIfxeRZ", "resumeLink": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "resumePreviewUrl": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_GOOGLE_DRIVE_ID", "clDriveId": "", "clLink": "ht