au pipelines that reduced reporting latency by over 40% while uncovering key drivers of funnel conversion and SLA performance. This blend of technical execution and stakeholder communication aligns closely with what University of Phoenix seeks in this position.</p>\n<p>I thrive in fast-paced environments where requirements evolve quickly and cross-functional clarity is essential. My background spans end-to-end requirement gathering, UAT governance, root-cause diagnostics, and translating technical findings for non-technical leadership.</p>\n<p>Thank you for your time and consideration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in SQL, Python, Tableau, and business analysis can support University of Phoenix's upcoming initiatives.</p>"}, {"sNo": "12", "sNoNum": 12, "resumeId": "c9018fde-3581-414f-92a4-e654615a78b0", "company": "United", "industry": "Airlines", "jobId": "GGN00002617", "title": "Analyst - Predictive Safety Analytics", "jd": "Description\nCorporate safety is integral for ensuring a safe workplace for our employees and travel experience for our customers. This role is responsible for supporting the development and implementation of a cohesive safety data strategy and supporting the Director of Safety Management Systems (SMS) in growing United\u2019s Corporate Safety predictive analytics capabilities.\n\nThis analyst will serve as a subject matter expert for corporate safety data analytics and predictive insight strategy and execution. This position will be responsible for supporting new efforts to deliver insightful data analysis and build new key metrics for use by the entire United Safety organization, with the goal of enabling data driven decision making and understanding for corporate safety. The analyst will be responsible for becoming the subject matter expert in several corporate safety specific data streams an", "location": "Gurugram, Haryana, India", "portal": "Company site", "jdUrl": "https://careers.united.com/us/en/c/corpor